\vspace{0.5cm}

Let $S = \{2, 3, 6, 12, 24, 36\}$ with the divisibility relation $\mid$.

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*), leftmargin=2em]
    \item Is $(S, \mid)$ a partial order?
    \item Is it a total order?
    \item Find all incomparable pairs.
    \item Find maximal and minimal elements.
\end{enumerate}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Solution:}}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{(a)} We verified in Example~1 that divisibility is reflexive,
antisymmetric, and transitive. So $(S, \mid)$ \textbf{is a partial order}.
\textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{(b)} Check comparability: $2 \mid 3$? No. $3 \mid 2$? No.
So $2$ and $3$ are \textbf{incomparable}. Therefore $(S, \mid)$
\textbf{is not a total order}. \textcolor{red}{$\times$}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{(c) Incomparable pairs:}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Pair} & \textbf{Reason} \\
\hline
$(2, 3)$ & $2\nmid 3$ and $3\nmid 2$ \\
\hline
$(3, 12)$ & $3\mid 12$ --- \textit{comparable} \\
\hline
$(12, 36)$ & $12\mid 36$ --- \textit{comparable} \\
\hline
$(24, 36)$ & $24\nmid 36$ and $36\nmid 24$ \\
\hline
$(12, 24)$ & $12\mid 24$ --- \textit{comparable} \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\textbf{Truly incomparable pairs:} $(2,3)$ and $(24,36)$.

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{(d)} From the divisibility structure:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em]
    \item \textbf{Minimal elements:} $2$ and $3$
          (nothing in $S$ divides $2$ or $3$ except themselves).
    \item \textbf{Maximal elements:} $24$ and $36$
          (neither $24$ nor $36$ divides the other, and nothing in $S$
          is divisible by both).
    \item \textbf{Least element:} Does not exist ($2$ and $3$ are incomparable).
    \item \textbf{Greatest element:} Does not exist ($24$ and $36$ are incomparable).
\end{itemize}

\vspace{0.5cm}




\begin{center}
